# Follow pawn vs camera snap

## Current stack (keep this)

Last known-good for **stationary + character in all directions**. Do not turn one of these off to debug another as a first pass.

- `enablePixelSnap` on, `enableSnapCompensate` **off** (no dest-slide)
- `CameraRig` independent `Mathf.Round` on camera right/up (no stored cell)
- `GameCamera` damp 0, `FollowPoint` height rounded to whole texels along `camera.up`
- Follow visual: `VisualSnap` ViewGlue with live `Round` of camera-relative origin
- `PlayerMotor` analog / camera-relative move + `RotateTowards`

**Looks locked:** stationary world, character walk in all directions. Pan is 1px steps.

**Still jittery:** the **environment** steps (noticeable going sideways). Dest-slide hides that but slides the hero too; user asked dest-slide off again.

## Do not re-run as a first pass

- **8-way / king-step camera snap**. Desyncs on direction change.
- Dest-slide on (slides the follow pawn).
- ViewGlue **pin**, dest-slide to whole screen pixels, 8-way motor + instant facing.
- Old F8 A/B: SkipHero, PinLockstep, PointSlide, FollowPlane, CallusClassic, SnapOnly, NoOutlines, SoftGround, extra hysteresis, ToonLit vertex snap, F8 Off/Snap/Callus.

## If asked to fix world stepping again

Dest-slide is the world fix. It moves the hero. Next is a new design (pixel expansion, or hero not in that present). Notes: `Assets/KylePixelator/Docs/README.md` (Follow pawn jitter).
